# love.audio

Provee un medio para reproducir **audio** mediante los parlantes/altavoces del usuario/oyente.

## Procedimientos y Funciones ~(métodos)~

+ love.audio.newSource
	* Crea una _fuente de audio_ desde los siguientes recursos :
		- un archivo de audio (Source) 
		- un archivo con datos de sónido (SoundData) 
		- un decoficador (Decoder).

	~~~
	[[ audioSource = love.audio.newSource( 
		resourceName -- String
		, sourceType -- String 
	) ]]
	bgm = love.audio.newSource("bgm.ogg", "stream")
	love.audio.play(bgm)
	~~~

+ love.audio.play
	* Reproduce la _fuente de audio_ (Source) especificado como parámetro.

	```
	love.audio.play( source )
	```

	~~~
	bgm = love.audio.newSource("bgm.ogg", "stream")
	love.audio.play(bgm)
	~~~

+ love.audio.pause
	* Pausa el audio en general o la fuente de audio en específico.

	```
	love.audio.pause( )
	love.audio.pause( source )
	```

+ love.audio.resume
	* Reanuda la reprodución de audio.
+ love.audio.rewind
	* Rebobina all playing audio.
+ love.audio.stop
	* Detiene currently played sources.
+ love.audio.getVolume
	* Returns the master volume.
+ love.audio.setVolume
	* Sets the master volume.
+ love.audio.getPosition
	* Returns the position of the listener.
+ love.audio.setPosition
	* Sets the position of the listener.
+ love.audio.getVelocity
	* Returns the velocity of the listener.
+ love.audio.setVelocity
	* Sets the velocity of the listener.
+ love.audio.getOrientation
	* Returns the orientation of the listener.
+ love.audio.setOrientation
	* Sets the orientation of the listener.
+ love.audio.getNumSources (< v0.9.0)
	* Gets the current number of simultaneously playing sources.
+ love.audio.getSourceCount (>= v0.9.0)
	* Gets the current number of simultaneously playing sources.
+ love.audio.getDistanceModel (>= v0.8.0)
	* Returns the distance attenuation model.
+ love.audio.setDistanceModel (>= v0.8.0)
	* Sets the distance attenuation model.
+ love.audio.getDopplerScale (>= v0.9.2)
	* Gets the global scale factor for doppler effects.
+ love.audio.setDopplerScale (>= v0.9.2)
	* Sets a global scale factor for doppler effects.

## Enumerables ~(enums)~ 

+ DistanceModel (>= v0.8.0)
	* The different distance models.
+ SourceType
	* Types of audio sources.
+ TimeUnit (>= v0.8.0)
	* Units that represent time.

